  "container_class_status": "canonical storage migrated; full class/API parity remains partial",
  "behavior": [
    "Removed simplified IndexedNode/owner Vec/bucket-index Vec and duplicated count/modulus/allocator. Actual BaseIndexedMapStorage owns both tables and count/allocator; flat IndexedMapNode retains real Next and signed Index. Canonical pointer graph owns nodes without a second registry or traversal order.",
    "All constructors, queries, mutation, copying and iteration route through actual storage. Native Swap updates node indices/table slots without hashing. Owned and borrowed Add reuse exactly one lookup hash. Empty membership performs no hash. Iteration borrows actual native index slots; all ended shared iterators compare equal.",
    "Native resize allocates index storage before hash replacement, hashes/relinks in old bucket/chain order, and commits actual base tables. A Rust Hash panic restores original Next links without calling user hash again. Node addresses remain stable.",
    "Heap-stable canonical metadata supports a readonly observer using short lock phases. No whole mutable base borrow or metadata lock spans key construction, assignment, hashing/equality or destruction. Observers copy opaque node identities, never dereference possibly destroyed nodes. Exchange preserves observer container identity.",
    "RemoveLast clears the last index slot before hashing, unlinks before key destruction/free, then decrements count. Clear calls key destructors in bucket/chain order with old count/index slots; it clears each head only after that chain, finishes count/hash-table phase, then index-table phase. Replacing allocator happens after all key callbacks.",
